{{- /*
  For modify_ templates, to manage a file but leave a few parts of it alone: a
  window position, a "last seen version", whatever the app rewrites by itself.

  Prints the file of the repo (.base, a path inside the source dir that starts
  with a dot so chezmoi doesn't treat it as a file of its own), except that every
  regex of .keep which matches in the file as it is on this machine (.stdin)
  gets the text of this machine instead. Everything else is copied byte for
  byte, so the app can rewrite the file and chezmoi sees no change as long as
  only those parts moved. A regex without a match on this machine (a new
  machine, or the app didn't write it yet) leaves the repo's text in place.

  Each regex is multiline: ^ and $ match at the line ends. Keep it to the part
  that changes, "key": "value" without the comma after it for JSON, so the
  commas around it come from the repo and the file stays valid.

  Use it from a modify_ template, see dot_pi/agent/modify_private_settings.json.
  The arguments are base (the path of the repo file), stdin (always
  .chezmoi.stdin) and keep (a list of regexes). Which files and regexes there
  are is in .chezmoidata/keep.yaml.
*/ -}}
{{- $out := include .base -}}
{{- range .keep -}}
{{-   $pattern := printf "(?m)%s" . -}}
{{-   $current := regexFind $pattern $.stdin -}}
{{-   if $current }}{{ $out = regexReplaceAllLiteral $pattern $out $current }}{{ end -}}
{{- end -}}
{{ $out -}}
